$ enola blame --help
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola blame [flags] <pattern> [repo_path|config_path]

Show when something entered the architecture and when it left.

The pattern is matched, case-insensitively, against the recorded facts — a
module or symbol name, a file path, or both endpoints of an edge. With
--findings it is matched against recorded findings instead.

With a shared store (--store, or history.shared_dir) the search runs over the
union of the local history and the store, and every event names where its
revision came from.

Only revisions whose contents are still stored can be searched; older ones
keep their summary line and are reported as unread rather than as absent.

Flags:
  -all
    	include working revisions (uncommitted trees)
  -findings
    	search the recorded findings instead of the facts
  -first
    	stop at the first appearance
  -full
    	print the whole matching line rather than its head
  -json
    	emit the events as JSON
  -store string
    	also search a shared history store (default: history.shared_dir)

Examples:
  # When did anything matching this enter or leave
  enola blame internal/auth

  # Only when it first appeared
  enola blame --first SessionStore

  # Search findings instead of facts
  enola blame --findings cycle

See also: enola help log, enola help show
